      "content": "This document outlines the Bloc 4 end-to-end MLOps presentation demo.\n\nVideo Title: End-to-End MLOps Defense Presentation\nLength: 5 minutes\n\nScript / Flow:\n1. Serving API & Inference (0:00 - 1:30)\n   - Run the API locally: `uvicorn src.app:app --port 8000`.\n   - Use `curl` or Postman to send a POST request with FX rates and Delay Days.\n   - Show the JSON response containing the prediction probability and binary risk assessment.\n\n2. Concept Drift Detection (1:30 - 3:00)\n   - Execute `python monitoring/monitor.py`.\n   - Demonstrate the script identifying a data drift using the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test against baseline distributions.\n   - Show the alert: \"Drift threshold exceeded (> 0.05).\"\n\n3. CI/CD & Automated Retraining (3:00 - 4:30)\n   - Show that the drift alert triggers `python retrain/run_retrain.py`.\n   - Display the retraining log: fetching new warehouse data, executing Random Forest, reporting improved F1-score, and overwriting the `.pkl` artifact.\n\n4. Conclusion (4:30 - 5:00)\n   - Confirm the new model is auto-loaded by FastAPI.\n   - Final successful prediction check to close the loop.",
